# Trivy vulnerability suppressions for the secure release gate.
#
# Add only an exact CVE ID, immediately preceded by one metadata comment line:
#   # owner=<github-handle>; review-by=<YYYY-MM-DD>; reason=<rationale>
#
# See docs/secure-release-gate.md for the approval process. The review-by date
# must be no more than 90 days out and cannot be in the past.

# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian has not shipped a perl fix (status affected); perl-base is a base-image dependency the Core Case Service never invokes (CMD is `node dist/index.js`), so the regex/Storable code path is unreachable at runtime. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2026-13221
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian marks this fix_deferred; perl-archive-tar ships with perl-base but is never invoked by the Core Case Service runtime. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2026-42496
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian has not shipped a perl fix (status affected); Storable is a perl-base component never invoked by the Core Case Service runtime. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2026-57433
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian has not shipped a perl fix (status affected); the affected regex compiler path is only reachable on 32-bit builds and perl-base is never invoked by the Core Case Service runtime. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2026-8376
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian marks this will_not_fix upstream; the affected zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6 zip-writing path in zlib1g is not exercised by the Core Case Service, which only links zlib for gzip/deflate. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2023-45853
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Fixed in tar 7.5.19, but this is npm's own bundled tar dependency inside the node:24-bookworm-slim base image (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar), not an application dependency; npm is never invoked in the running container. Re-check on the next node:24-bookworm-slim digest bump.
CVE-2026-59873
# owner=platform-security; review-by=2026-11-17; reason=Debian has not shipped a fix (status affected; still present on the latest python:3.13-slim-bookworm digest); the overflow requires executing arbitrary attacker-controlled SQL, and the GL-coding service never imports Python's sqlite3 module or otherwise executes SQL against SQLite. Re-check on the next python:3.13-slim-bookworm digest bump.
CVE-2025-7458
